#: ../../source/docs/common-batt-watt-max.rst:5
#: 66c82788e1e7408a85702716ff37ef8b
msgid "Limiting Maximum Battery Power Draw"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-batt-watt-max.rst:7
#: 8fb3e77e17ae4cbea891e9ef3920022a
msgid "Often, long range vehicles utilize lower C rating batteries to maximize battery power to weight ratio. Unfortunately, some situations, especially QuadPlane transitions which have full throttle power applied to forward motors during the transition, can cause excessive battery voltage sag with lower C rated batteries. This can lead to permanent damage in some kinds of batteries (LiPo for example) if the cell voltage drops too low. In addition, this can cause premature battery failsafes, or even crashes. This topic discusses ways to limit the maximum power draw from batteries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-batt-watt-max.rst:10
#: 3c6feb0cc503404c9e994c33b1b22fd6
msgid "Methods to Limit Maximum Power Draw"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-batt-watt-max.rst:12
#: 4e55b2c8104f44cba0983372a8755783
msgid "The first and simplest is to restrict :ref:`THR_MAX<THR_MAX>` to a lower value. This limits the maximum throttle applied in throttle controlled modes (AUTO, FBWB, CRUISE, etc.). Unfortunately, while this could be used to limit maximum power to the forward motors in a QuadPlane transition, it will also limit it in normal fixed wing throttle controlled modes also, when the VTOL motors are not running and adding to the total instantaneous battery power being drawn."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-batt-watt-max.rst:14
#: bd7f260d0bac461ab0ba441346a43c2c
msgid "A better way is to use one or more of the power limiting parameters:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-batt-watt-max.rst:16
#: 9e24ab34d875437ab9951f4d9a59b362
msgid ":ref:`BATT_WATT_MAX<BATT_WATT_MAX>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-batt-watt-max.rst:18
#: 582595d57adf4cbaa915765eb90ad5a9
msgid "The :ref:`BATT_WATT_MAX<BATT_WATT_MAX>` parameter (``BATTx_WATT_MAX``, for any additional batteries) to limit the total instantaneous power that can be drawn from the battery(s) by the forward motors. This will help issues during QuadPlane transitions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-batt-watt-max.rst:20
#: 52e6a7e4ef504346af2bc9f89a5a6018
msgid "If battery wattage (voltage * current) exceeds this value then the system will reduce max throttle (:ref:`THR_MAX<THR_MAX>`, :ref:`TKOFF_THR_MAX<TKOFF_THR_MAX>` and :ref:`THR_MIN<THR_MIN>` for reverse thrust) to be below :ref:`BATT_WATT_MAX<BATT_WATT_MAX>`. If power demand is reduced, the max throttle will slowly grow back to :ref:`THR_MAX<THR_MAX>` (or :ref:`TKOFF_THR_MAX<TKOFF_THR_MAX>` ) and/or :ref:`THR_MIN<THR_MIN>`, even if demanding the current max but as long as power remains under the watt max. Use 0 (default) to disable this feature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-batt-watt-max.rst:22
#: 05dbfdca5cc045ccba72c9ff80e946d8
msgid "Since this limit is applied to the throttle slowly (~10%/second), it may not react fast enough in some situations to prevent battery sag at the beginning of transition. Setting the :ref:`THR_SLEWRATE<THR_SLEWRATE>` to 50% or less per second to prevent rapid application of maximum forward throttle at the beginning of transition, will help prevent this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-batt-watt-max.rst:24
#: f0e8557683be42f6b4c1f0b2f045cccf
msgid "This only affects the forward motors, VTOL motors are unaffected by :ref:`BATT_WATT_MAX<BATT_WATT_MAX>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-batt-watt-max.rst:26
#: f574fd97cd0141999265c01fc0df4956
msgid ":ref:`Q_M_BAT_CURR_MAX<Q_M_BAT_CURR_MAX>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-batt-watt-max.rst:28
#: bffeb1a42d4c45988da2bfa1296eca02
msgid "This can be used to limit the maximum current when the VTOL motors are active. Power will be reduced to the VTOL motors to prevent exceeding this value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-batt-watt-max.rst:30
#: 61d42cf995404ea9b33d6c12cee1d1e1
msgid ":ref:`Q_M_BAT_VOLT_MIN<Q_M_BAT_VOLT_MIN>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-batt-watt-max.rst:32
#: 0116226c63254761b30d44c89bb5c663
msgid "This has two effects if non-zero. First, it sets the lower limit for thrust scaling versus voltage. If :ref:`Q_M_BAT_VOLT_MAX<Q_M_BAT_VOLT_MAX>` is non-zero, then voltage compensation is applied to throttle to offset battery voltage variations on thrust. Second, it sets a lower limit on battery voltage sag by predicting the throttle value that would cause this, using an estimate of battery internal resistance calculated during flight. It will limit current applied to the VTOL motors to prevent this from occurring. If :ref:`Q_M_BAT_CURR_MAX<Q_M_BAT_CURR_MAX>` is also  non-zero, then it will use the lower of the two limits, the one set by :ref:`Q_M_BAT_CURR_MAX<Q_M_BAT_CURR_MAX>` or predicted internally using :ref:`Q_M_BAT_VOLT_MIN<Q_M_BAT_VOLT_MIN>`  as the minimum voltage sag target."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-batt-watt-max.rst:34
#: 47e1b16af5fe4a2f921e7c71b09a848c
msgid "the battery used for monitoring and the battery resistance estimate is determined by  :ref:`Q_M_BAT_IDX<Q_M_BAT_IDX>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-batt-watt-max.rst:36
#: 25dc976e46634f02be782df1eb201e94
msgid "Setting :ref:`Q_M_BAT_CURR_MAX<Q_M_BAT_CURR_MAX>` to 150% of hover current is a good starting point, while 3.3V * number of cells is a good value for :ref:`Q_M_BAT_VOLT_MIN<Q_M_BAT_VOLT_MIN>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-batt-watt-max.rst:41
#: 1c77cdf7ee924e2ab9ff57deb35e71e9
msgid "How to Set Max Watts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-batt-watt-max.rst:42
#: 686ac55dac5f465f82f4a4ccd29e62b3
msgid "By examining a post run dataflash log, and noting anywhere excessive battery voltage sag first occurs, you can take the battery voltage and current at that point, multiply to obtain the power, and set the :ref:`BATT_WATT_MAX<BATT_WATT_MAX>` to below that value. 80% to 70% of the value noted at the sag point would be a good value to start with."
msgstr ""
